"q-149634/selection/4fa830bda994f89067ddecaf273e4fa78aa4d8447b6388b70cafa0fc166e6f67" "q-149634/selection/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149634" :question/id #uuid "4cb6dc3e-d65f-5a78-889b-bf2893192b18" :question/math-academy-id "q-149634" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,7]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[-3,-2]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}4({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[2,7].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=7-2 & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $j,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{x}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}\\,+\\,{y}_{0})({y}_{1}\\,-\\,{y}_{0})\\,+\\,({y}_{2}\\,+\\,{y}_{1})({y}_{2}\\,-\\,{y}_{1})\\,+\\,⋯\\,+\\,({y}_{n}\\,+\\,{y}_{n-1})({y}_{n}\\,-\\,{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(-2)^{2}-(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}=4\\cdot 5\\cdot (-5)=-100.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-149634/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149634"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149629/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "8a5b1c81-d3df-5121-ac23-82ff8a9510bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149629/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "88e08c79-f188-5d52-a09b-29e785491666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149629/selection/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" :answer/id #uuid "2df7bd4b-9fbb-5d05-959c-50e8ca2048f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149629/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "0f8a5b4b-138f-5228-bf85-4b42fd5d0dea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149629/selection/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7" :answer/id #uuid "2d066937-2c4a-5e6e-889e-a70d7760bdd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149629/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac53f04e-3c07-5ae4-804a-c97cbd11393b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149629/selection/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" :answer-field/choices ["q-149629/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-149629/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-149629/selection/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" "q-149629/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" "q-149629/selection/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149629" :question/id #uuid "1b4ef090-1288-5ca1-833a-7ba30aaefd89" :question/math-academy-id "q-149629" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,6]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[4,6]$\n\nCalculate  ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[4,6].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=6-4=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we can evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={6}^{2}-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=32\\cdot 2=64.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-149629/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149629"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149635/selection/8ca4b7a1e89c730869f48c3a3ace0473b36e7c19c70ef8efef65592fedc719dd" :answer/id #uuid "fb3d1053-437d-5056-aaf8-c5647d3d89cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149635/selection/2bb3e52c9706ad091d61ac1e0fe07e0e3f5ec51850a26a5c75350df1ddfc3e57" :answer/id #uuid "50342f8c-5817-58d9-b183-89df4ae186f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-54" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149635/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "f803a49e-8f89-5b07-aa7d-b449fe539ff6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149635/selection/d6944c4d51ee6e8916d5e2815a8478bad91a2f9e9e9bcd499b503b9fbcb165ab" :answer/id #uuid "06425ad5-3904-50c1-a003-4f1745ffca30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149635/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer/id #uuid "c45147b2-7c43-5aec-829c-75f029c7f626" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149635/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd031717-924c-53a1-906f-5f362af89b01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149635/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer-field/choices ["q-149635/selection/8ca4b7a1e89c730869f48c3a3ace0473b36e7c19c70ef8efef65592fedc719dd" "q-149635/selection/2bb3e52c9706ad091d61ac1e0fe07e0e3f5ec51850a26a5c75350df1ddfc3e57" "q-149635/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" "q-149635/selection/d6944c4d51ee6e8916d5e2815a8478bad91a2f9e9e9bcd499b503b9fbcb165ab" "q-149635/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149635" :question/id #uuid "41d30f3a-6e37-555f-9aae-459b7e89604b" :question/math-academy-id "q-149635" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[-4,-1]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[8,9]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}-3({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n-3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[8,9].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=9-8 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}\\,+\\,{x}_{0})({x}_{1}\\,-\\,{x}_{0})\\,+\\,({x}_{2}\\,+\\,{x}_{1})({x}_{2}\\,-\\,{x}_{1})\\,+\\,⋯\\,+\\,({x}_{m}\\,+\\,{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}\\,-\\,{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}-(-4)^{2} \\\\  & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n-3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=(-3)\\cdot (-15)\\cdot 1=45.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-149635/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149635"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9482"] :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1, 2]$\n\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 3]$\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n {3} \\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j,$ where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\Delta x_i$ and $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[-1, 2]$ and $[2,3]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =2-(-1)=3, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =3-2=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n3 \\sum_{i=1}^m \\Delta x_i \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1 = 9.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6117"] :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[4, 6]$\n\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 6]$\n\nCalculate  $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j,$ where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[2, 6].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=6-2=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we can evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}\\,+\\,{x}_{0})({x}_{1}\\,-\\,{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}\\,+\\,{x}_{1})({x}_{2}\\,-\\,{x}_{1})+({x}_{m}\\,+\\,{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}\\,-\\,{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={6}^{2}-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at \n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j = 20\\cdot 4 = 80.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
